mission "A Sea Without Masters"
    name "A Sea Without Masters"
    description "Take the articles to Port Royal and attend the final council."
    source "Havana"
    destination "Port Royal"
    reward 2200
    speaker offer "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker visit "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker complete "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    to offer
        has "Ashcombe's Last Wager: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `With Ashcombe defeated, the free captains must decide what becomes of the Company ports and its captured crews.`
            `Some island councils want the Company dissolved. Others want its warehouses returned to the people who built them. Bonny insists no new governor should inherit the same power under a different flag.`
            `The final journey is not a battle. Carry the signed harbour articles to Port Royal, where the captains and island councils will establish a shared sea charter.`
            choice
                `"You have my attention. What needs doing first?"`
                    goto accept_job
                `"Who stands to gain if the truth stays buried?"`
                    goto more_details
                `"I have no wish to become a pawn in someone else's quarrel."`
                    goto decline_job
            label more_details
                `Commodore Anne Bonny leans closer and speaks plainly. "The final journey is not a battle. Carry the signed harbour articles to Port Royal, where the captains and island councils will establish a shared sea charter."`
                choice
                    `"All right. I will follow the evidence."`
                        goto accept_job
                    `"My answer has not changed. I will not sail."`
                        goto decline_job
            label accept_job
                `The Havana harbourmaster gives you the signed articles. “You have brought us a quieter sort of victory, captain. Let it last longer than the last one.”`
                accept
            label decline_job
                `Bonny folds the chart and gives you a level look. "Fair enough, captain. I would rather have your ship on the course, but I will not press a captain who has already made up their mind."`
                close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Sea Without Masters. Take the articles to Port Royal and attend the final council."
    on visit
        conversation
            `The free captains and island councils sign the new articles. The Meridian Company is dissolved, its ports restored, and its crews given the choice to return home or sail under fair contracts.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `The sea remains wide and dangerous, but no single company or governor can claim it. Your chart now shows thirty-three harbours across six island regions open to exploration.`
        log "Completed A Sea Without Masters. Received 2200 gold. The sea remains wide and dangerous, but no single company or governor can claim it. Your chart now shows thirty-three harbours across six island regions open to exploration."
